2 SURN Olofsdotter (Hjulstaätt)
2 _MARNM Olofsdotter (Hjulstaätt)
1 SEX F
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Margareta Olofsdotter (Hjulstaätt)=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Hjulstaätten is a modern name for an Uppland savior family during the 15th century with Hjulsta in Enköpings-Näs parish in Uppland as the family estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hjulsta%C3%A4tten Hjulstaätten Family, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT Crest: three five-petalled roses barred 
2 CONT The coat of arms was previously described by Jan Raneke as three six-pointed white stars bar-wise on a blue field, which the medieval genealogist Kaj Janzon has refuted in the Genealogists' yearbook from 2005. the coat of arms wit
2 CONC h the three roses can be seen in SDHK no: 14646 ( Swedish Diplomatarium's main catalog of medieval letters ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Selected members=
2 CONT
2 CONT The underling in Uppland and the bailiff of Fjärhundraland Haral in Hiwlistom . (Harald Olofsson i Hjulsta) in 1420 transferred the farm Hjulsta from Uppsala cathedral [ 3 ] . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Olofsson and his second wife Katarina Fadersdotter are mentioned in 1377 in a letter to Drotsen Bo Jonsson Grip [ 4 ] and the last time in 1386. In his first marriage to an unknown woman, Harald had a son:
2 CONT Olof Haraldsson (died in the 1430s), bought estates in 1393 for 1140 marks from Sten Bosson (Night and Day) , who called Olof his lovable sven . 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1- Olof was married to a Katarina Skäringsdotter (died before 1420), daughter of Skäring Iliansson (future swine balkvis) and Ragnhild Johansdotter. In 1396, Olof Haraldsson exchanged land with Strängnäs cathedral and in the doc
2 CONC ument from the exchange deed, Olof has used his seal, which is why we do not know the colors of the coat of arms, which carried three five-petalled roses in a beam.Olof Haraldsson was district chief in Hölebo no later than 1410, a
2 CONC nd is mentioned in 1417 when he exchanged land with Henning Bolt . In 1420 he uses a seal again, which was then changed to a beam with the three roses. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Skäring Olofsson
2 CONT
2 CONT * 2- Cecilia Olofsdotter, married to the lawman in Östergötland, Gert Jonsson (star) .
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ficke Olofsson, married to Elin Nilsdotter till Ängsö ( Night and Day )
2 CONT * '''Margareta Olofsdotter, married before 1437 to Gustav Laurensson (Ängaätten)''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT After Ficke Olofsson's death, his widow inherited Hjulsta, who after she remarried Father Ulfsson ( Sparre av Hjulsta og Ängsö ) passed into the Sparreätt, which after the farm Hjulsta , is called Sparre av Hjulsta och Ängsö .
