1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of King Charles VIII of Sweden and Kristina Abrahamsdotter
2 CONT * Anna, a natural daughter of Carl VIII  Knutsson and his mistress Christina, whom he explained to his real wife in 1470 on the cot. Anna married the chieftain at Westerås Castle in 1450   , Håkan Svensson Bölja. King Karl VIII's 
2 CONC  daughter Anna, can be found in Notes on Swedish women (Stockholm, PG Berg, 1864), now scanned at Project Runeberg. 
2 CONT * Karl Knutsson was born in October 1408 or 1409, at Ekholmen Castle, the son of Knut Tordsson (Bonde), knight and member of the privy council (riksråd), and Margareta Karlsdotter (Sparre av Tofta), the only daughter and heiress o
2 CONC f Charles Ulvsson, Lord of Tofta. His father Knut was first cousin of Erik Johansson Vasa's father. His first marriage, in 1428, to Birgitta Turesdotter (Bielke) (died 1436) gave him his daughter Christina. His second marriage, in
2 CONC  1438, to Catherine (Gumsehuvud, died in 1450) produced his second daughter Magdalena, who married Ivar Axelsson (Tott). He also had two children by his third wife (and former mistress) Christina Abrahamsdotter, Anna and Karl. His
2 CONC  father was said by contemporary legends to descend from a younger brother of King Eric IX (Saint Eric). His mother, an important heiress, descended from Jarl Charles the Deaf and consequently from some ancient Folkunge earls of S
2 CONC weden, as well as from Ingegerd Knutsdotter, a daughter of Canute IV of Denmark and Adela of Flanders.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000006588594080&photo_id=6000000118119715821&position=1 '''Anna Karlsdotter (Bonde) is listed in the Granfelt fran Dal - Mörner af Tuna, Volume 2, page 196 as the d
2 CONC otter of  King Karl Knutsson Bonde.''']
