1 OCCU Häradshövding, Väpnare, riksråd Erikstad (Stenbock), väpnare, riksrådoch häradshövding i Sunnerbo
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stenbock,_%C3%A4ldre_%C3%A4tten
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=20066
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof Jönsson Stenbock (Äldre ätten), Väpnare, Riksråd och Häradshövding
2 CONT
2 CONT Blev va 46 år
2 CONT
2 CONT Född omkring 1409 Tofta, Jönköping
2 CONT
2 CONT Död 1455 Vittaryd (G)
2 CONT
2 CONT Far Jöns "Skytte" Stenbock 1348-1391
2 CONT
2 CONT Mor Kerstin Birgersdotter Trole 1359-
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Sestrid Knutsdottor Barun (Körning) -1441
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Göstaf Olofsson Stenbock 1441-1492
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Olofsson Stenbock -1488
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia Ol ätten, var Olof Jönssons senare hustru Margareta Svensdotter Krumme, dotter vtill Sven Bäk och Botild Klausdotter Apellegardofsdotter Stenbock
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Margareta Svensdotter Krumme 1416-1484
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigsel efter 1441
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Märta Olofsdotter Stenbock -1486
2 CONT
2 CONT Stenbock den äldre ätten
2 CONT
2 CONT Till Eriksatd
2 CONT
2 CONT Riddare, riksråd och häradshövding i Sunnerbo härad
2 CONT
2 CONT Blev innebränd, sannolikt under kriget 1455
2 CONT
2 CONT Enligt Pontus Möllers redovisning av Stenbock, äldre ätten, var Olof Jönssons senare hustru Margareta Svensdotter Krumme, dotter till Sven Bäk och Botild Klausdotter Apellegard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oklart vilken av Jöns hustrur som var moder till Olof.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Stamfader för de äldre stenbockarna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Häradshövding i Sunnerbo,riddare och riksråd.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.svenskgeografi.se/laen/joenkoeping/18976-sunnerbo.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.svenskgeografi.se/laen/kronoberg/64238-erikstad.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Brann inne i kriget mot danskarna.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olof blev innebränd under kriget 1455. Tidigast nämnd 1406. Han blev mellan 1408 och 2/2 1426 Häradshövding i Sunnerbo hd i Småland till den 17/3 1445. Hövitsman 6/5 1442 i Sunnerbo. Nämnes bland riksens råd och män tidigast 1435 
2 CONC men som riksråd endast 1440. Daterade brev år 1406 på sin fars forna sätesgård Ekornarp i Berga sn i Sunnerbo hd men hade 4/9 1444 och 8/6 1451 som sätesgård Erikstad i Vittaryds sn i samma hd. Hade landbohemman i Sunnerbo hd och 
2 CONC i Västbo, Östbo hd i Småland och i Fjäre och Himle hd i Halland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Karrie Welborn, Adding source: https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Stenbock,_%C3%A4ldre_%C3%A4tten
2 CONT
2 CONT TABLE 2
2 CONT Capricorn older family.png
2 CONT Olof Jönsson (son of Jösse skytte, tab. 1). Earliest mentioned in 1406. Became between 1408 and 2.2 1426 district chief in Sunnerbo hd in Småland, which he was still 17.3 1445; no successor can be appointed until several years aft
2 CONC er his death; it is probably a misspelling, as on 6.5 1442 he is called Hövitsman in Sunnerbo. Mentioned among the council and men of the kingdom as early as 1435, but as a councilor only in 1440. Dated 1406 letter on his father's
2 CONC  former seat Ekomarp in Berga sn, Sunnerbo hd, but had at least 4.9 1444 and 8.6 1451 as seat Erikstad in Vittaryds sn in the same hd. Was burned, probably during the war in 1455. In 1441 was widowed by Sestrid, daughter of the kn
2 CONC ight Knut Eringisleson ( Barun ) also called Knut April and Bengta Matsdotter (star). Remarried to Margareta Svensdotter ( Krumme), who still lived on 26.2 1484 at Sunnaryd in Bolmsö sn, Västbo hd, was the daughter of Sven Bäk and
2 CONC  Botild Klausdotter ( Apellegard ) and remarried Christiern Drake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Jösse Olsson, 1441, died 1488, courtier, councillor. See tab. 3 .
2 CONT 1. Gustav Olsson, 1441, died 1492, knight, councillor. See tab. 4 .
2 CONT 1. Knut Olsson or Knut April. Enrolled in Nov. 1437 at the University of Rostock and in the winter of 1439 at the University of Leipzig, where he became a baccalaureus in the summer of 1440 and a master's degree in the spring of 1
2 CONC 442. Became a canon in Uppsala on 30.4.1445 at the latest. Was 8.3 1449 canon in both Uppsala and Linköping and vicar in Stockholm, ordained 18.3 s.å. to deacon and 12.4. so. to priest. Resigned from the vicarship between 25.1 145
2 CONC 1 and 1453. Died between 1455 and 1475. He had an illegitimate son named Olof).
2 CONT 1. Eringisl Olsson. Died no earlier than 1441.
2 CONT 2. Anund Olsson. Died childless.
2 CONT 2. Cecilia Olsdotter. Still alive in 1479. Married to Sven Pik, who cannot be dated later than 1462. Remarried no later than 1479 to the district chief Philippus Karlsson ( Mälsåkerätten ) at Mälsåker in Ytterselö sn, Selebo hd in
2 CONC  Södermanland, who was still alive on 14.12.1497.
2 CONT 2. Claus Olsson. Probably identical to the person with this name whom King Karl Knutsson sent to Roslagen in 1469 to gather people against Erik Karlsson's ( Vasa ) rebellion, but who was beaten and captured by him at Knutby church
2 CONC . In that case, became a knight between 1469 and 1471.
2 CONT 2. Märta Olsdotter. Still alive 12.3 1486 and was then married to Jöns Persson ( Ulfsax ), who then had Håringe in Bolmsö sn, Västbo hd as a seat farm and was still alive in 1488.
2 CONT 2. Estrid Olsdotter. Died unmarried.
