2 CONC e and a female monastery in Vadstena and that her words became one of the many (among others, the Dominican Order), which was housed under the Augustine rule. On Aug. 5, 1370, a bullock was issued for this. The definitive affirmat
2 CONC ion of the "St. Augustini Salvation Order", which is the abbreviated official name, was first issued after B's death by Urban VII. She has to settle for having a male and a female monastery in Vadstena and that her words became on
