2 CONT == Helga Bengtsdotter (winged arrow), Wikipedia==
2 CONT
2 CONT Helga Bengtsdotter , died in 1393, was a Swedish landowner. She was the daughter of Bengt Elofsson (winged arrow) . She was first married to ten-army batsman Sune Jonsson (Boat) , of Erengisle Sunesson's lineage. Widow at least si
2 CONC nce October 12, 1339 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Helga Bengtsdotter received from Sune Jonsson land in a morning gift in Ashland in Östergötland , which she, when the marriage was childless, donated to Vadstena monastery and received land in Östra hered in Småland and owned othe
2 CONC r land in Södra Vedbo hered and Västra hered in the same landscape, as well as in Aska, Dals and Valkebo, in Östergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The donation letter was sealed by the issuer as well as the knights Earl Erengisle Sunesson , Karl Ulfsson by Tofta , the team in Uppland, Bengt Filipsson , Birger Ulfsson and Sten Bengtsson .
2 CONT
2 CONT The second time married in 1350 to Magnus Knutsson (Aspenäsätt) .
2 CONT
2 CONT She was buried January 8, 1393 in Vadstena Monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'''- https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helga_Bengtsdotter_(vingad_pil)
