2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Lindorm Björnsson (Vinge)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Född:	cirka 1435
2 CONT * Död:	1499 (59-68) Borgholm, Öland, Sverige 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Yrke:	Lagman i Västergötland, Kanik 
2 CONT * Från 1476 var han häradshövding i Vilske härad och riksråd 1478. Vidare var Lindorm lagman i  Västergötland 1481-1498 och hövitsman på Örestens borg 1486-1488. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son till Björn Nilsson (Vinge) och Kristina Abjörnsdotter (Bagge af Berga) 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Make till. 
2 CONT * Cecilia Simonsdotter Båt giftemål 1463 i Lödöse 
2 CONT * Birgitta Mårtensdotter Svan giftemål 1467 
2 CONT * Christina Laurensdotter 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Fader till Knut Lindormsson (Vinge), till Sjögerås; Ana Sparre; Laurens Lindormsson Vinge; Hans Lindormsson Vinge; Birgitta Lindormsdotter Vinge; Kristina Lindormsdotter Vinge och Märta Lindormsdotter Vinge 
2 CONT * Broder till Abjörn Björnsson (Vinge); Olof Björnsson (Vinge) och Nils Björnsson (Vinge) 
2 CONT * Halvbroder till Ingeborg Bjørnsdotter Vinge 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT In Lödöse there was a wedding in 1463 between the squire Lindorm Björnsson and Cecilia Simonsdotter.
2 CONT Cecilia died childless and Lindorm remarried in 1467 to Birgitta Mårtensdotter Svan.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1476 he was district judge in Vilske härad and privy councilor in 1478. Lindorm was also a lawman in Västergötland 1481-1498 and courtier at Öresten castle 1486-1488.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lindorm was probably killed at Borgholm on Öland in 1499. His seal stamp has been found there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Middle Ages in Bierka and Swnd (David Myrehed ISBN978-91-633-7189-9)
2 CONT
2 CONT Medeltidsbreven
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 27266
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14580629, Tingvalla
2 CONT Content: Olof Björnsson, judge in Värmland, issues at the county council in Tingvalla, in the presence of bishop Bengt in Skara and others, court letter in the dispute between wife Katarina (Birgersdotter) in Åby (Landa parish) in
2 CONC  Kullings härad and Otto Torbjörnsson, bailiff in Värmland, regarding 3 farms, namely Skåra and "Lysogh" (wrong for Härtsöga) in Grava parish in Kils (now Karlstads) county, in Östrasysslet in Värmland, and Dåverud in Millesvik pa
2 CONC rish in Näs County; Katarina's father (Birger - happiness in ms) Folkesson had inherited these farms from his "brother" Måns Torbjörnsson. According to testimony by Niklis Niklisson, Niklis Gunnarsson and others, these farms had n
2 CONC ever been pledged to Claus Niklisson (bailiff of Värmland 1440-46), as Otto Torbjörnsson claims, but Claus Niklisson had, when Catherine's father died, illegally deprived her of said farms. Olof Björnsson grants his wife Katarina 
2 CONC and her heirs the farms. 12 lay judges are listed, among them the squire Lindorm Björnsson, Pelle i Ramstad and Måns Bok (=Buk).
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more on https://sok.riksarkivet.se/Sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=14612
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 28086
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14630124, Lödöse
2 CONT
2 CONT Content: Lindorm Björnsson (Vinge) gives to his wife Cecilia, Simon Gudmundsson's daughter, in morning gift Gunntorp in Skövde sn and Mökered in the same sn (now in S:t Peters sn) in Ale hd, a gd in Vittene (Lena sn) and Rakåsa in
2 CONC  Eggvena (now in Fölene) sn in Kullings hd, in addition Fors (now Forsvik) in Botilsäters sn and Averstad in the same sn (now in Ölseruds sn) in Näs' hd. Witnesses were Mr Tideman, canon in Skara, and Jon Andersson, village bailif
2 CONC f in Lödöse. Twelve fasts are enumerated.
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 28723
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14670525, Sjögerås Content: Lindorm Björnsson gives his house Birgitta Mårtensdotter as a morning gift Fors and "Albirstadha" in Näs hd in Värmland and several homesteads in Västergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT P.S. Who is this Lindorm Björnsson?
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 30018
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14760000, Sjögerås Content: Björn Petersson and Torsten Björnsson have together with all their friends and kinsmen been gathered in Vilske härad at the courthouse on Ullene heath, when the well-born man Lindorm Björnsson e
2 CONC ntered into a settlement with Jöns Petersson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rd Lage Posse, Otte Torbjörnsson, Karl Bengtsson, Peter Bonde, Bertil Petersson and Björn Bengtsson seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT SDHK-nr: 31037
2 CONT
2 CONT Issued: 14820114, Skara Content: Lindorm Björnsson, judge in Västergötland, adjudicates in dispute between Birger Bertilsson and Helge in Tega on the one hand and Jon Björnsson on the other about Jon's sister's inheritance from hi
2 CONC s parents, whereby Jon Björnsson is awarded the estates, namely. Djupsås, Krogstorp, Spjutstorp etc. (Essunga sn, Barne hd) and Birger Bertilsson their money.
2 CONT
