1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=SDHK+4420&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_4420&tab=post SDHK no: 4420]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1338 June 13'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Birger Bek gives his wife Ingrid estates in Sjöaryd and Hårdnäs as a gift tomorrow which, in case the marriage becomes childless, can be redeemed by the family with 24 marks of silver if he dies first, and with 20 marks of silver 
2 CONC if she dies first. But if the spouses have children, these estates shall accrue to them in maternity.
2 CONT
2 CONT To all who see this written Birgerus bek. Greetings in the Lord forever Know that I have given my beloved consort Ingrid for honor and reason of dower, which is commonly called hinderdagsgif, my goods in Sioarydh and Hardanes on s
2 CONC uch a condition that if I happen to die without children, then my heirs for twenty-four pure marks have the right to redeem them, but if she happens to die first without children, then the aforesaid goods are redeemed for twenty p
2 CONC ure marks, if indeed we happen to have children, the aforementioned goods are to be theirs for marriage and not patrimony. In testimony of which fact the seals. namely. beloved of my mother, Swenonis bek the Great Finn, one with m
2 CONC y seal, are appended to the present. Dated in the year of our Lord. M°. 300°. 300. 8th Saturday before Botulfi
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The issuer and his mother Gymnid, Sven Bek, Magnus Månsson seal.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/4420.pdf '''SEAL''']  The seal: No. 1, "S. Gymmnidis” (a rose, without a shield); No. 2, "S. Svenonis Bæk”, nobly (fish on a slanted beam); No. 3, "S. Mangni monson” (the shield divided, t
2 CONC he upper part blank, in the lower a bent branch with leaves); No. 4, "S. Birgeri Bec (oblique beam with indistinct transverse lines).
