2 CONT About Holger Andersen Green, for Aarup Gaard  in Tamdrup Bisgård  During Stjernholm County  to Årupgård (Tamdrup)  Known 1603-21  Though he looks like being true born son after Anders Grøn, he looks for being named after Holger Ro
2 CONC senkrantz. For "homage" in 1608, he stepped over the peasantry and probably married into this. | Got 4.August 1627 Royal. confirmation to possess "Aarup Gaard" Free of genuine and work, while his son Thing scribe lived with him.  
2 CONC The first historically known Jens Green mentioned 1325.Hans son is possible Jep Grøn  whose son Jens Grøn mentioned 1411.En of his three sons Niels Grøn mentioned 1468  a son of Niels Grøn was possible Jens Grøn or "gammle" Jens G
2 CONC røn married Maren Andersdatter  from Voergaard in Vendsyssel Jens Grøns son Erik grøn mentioned in 1509 for Voergaard .One of his  sons was probably Anders Grøn, mentioned from 1536, got Tamdrup bisgaard at Horsens in the leasing 
2 CONC of  crown and died 1580.Sønnen Holger Andersen green lived in Bisgaard and had also Aarup Gaard  in the same parish, but seemed even before 1608 to be entered into the peasantry .Hans two sons were  herredsfoged Anders Holgersen g
2 CONC reen in Aarup Gaard and Provst Erik Holgersen green in Vissing  Vorladegaard, pastor 1628-1664.Jeg assume that Johanne Grøn is the daughter of Jens Grøn mentioned  1567-90 in the head (now Manor in Ørridslev parish) Gmane Nielsdat
2 CONC ter; they were both dead before 08/03/1596  as following sun bestows altar candlesticks in rridslev church for their funeral and tenant place in  altergulvet.Jens Green may be the grandson of old Jens Grøn. "Young Jens Grøn" s son
2 CONC  was Niels  Grøn who in 1593 was bailiff in Skanderborg Len, then had a farm in Borup in Kattrup parish to establish  as he in 1608 with his wife got life letter paa.1601 he donated prædkestolen in Kattrup, died  1612, buried in K
2 CONC attrup church where there is a worn tombstones with characters and hoved.Borupgaard now o.  40 acres hartk. (1938) he remembers since the region as "the evil Bond King", 1.ggmKirsten  Nielsdatter, d before 1612. 2.Ggm Ingeborg Gjo
2 CONC rdsdatter Galt d.1637, was from Tyrreestrup, lived in 1634  in a farm in Tolstrup, as widow "the unfree Niels Grøn" .Niels Green has well then followed his brother  Sejer Bonde as bailiff in Skanderborg.  Dean Filtenborg points to
2 CONC  Jens grøn in the main as the father of Johanne Grøn  Jens Grøn is samfrænde in switched after Anders Bonde and Barbara Gødesdatter 
2 CONT
