1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I2515&tree=2 Peder Skram (born about 1503 - July 11, 1581). Board of Governors, Admiral. Married to Elsebeth, who was a daughter of Rigmarian Tyge Crab. During 
2 CONC their long marriage, Peder Skram and Elsebe Krabbe received a total of 18 children; 7 sons and 11 daughters. Three of the daughters died at birth and only one of the sons and seven of the daughters survived their parents. Alone in
2 CONC  1566, four of their sons died. Participated with Henrik Gøje in the field in Sweden and saved at Uppsala Mogens Gyldenstierne. When Christian 2. was expelled, Peder Skram was at the siege of Copenhagen in 1523. In 1532, he sailed
2 CONC  with a small navy to Norway to find Christian 2's 5 ships. These brought him at Tønsberg and rescued Mogens Gyldenstier in Akershus. Duke Christian sent him at the request of Gustav Vasa to Stockholm in 1535 to command the Swedis
2 CONC h Navy, which, together with Danish and Prussian ships, would break Lübeck's power. Became a leader of all naval wards, assisted by the Swedish admiral Per Månsson. After killing the opponent's fleet at Bornholm, he continued to L
2 CONC illebælt, where he destroyed some hostile ships. By doing so, he secured Johan Rantza's transfer of troops to Zealand after the victory in the Battle of Øksnebjerg. Peder Skram then entered Langeland and Korsør. From July 1535 he 
2 CONC blocked the fleet Copenhagen and Malmö. He was injured but returned to the blockade and participated in surrender on July 29, 1536. At Christian 3's coronation in 1537 he was turned into a knight and in 1539 admitted to the counci
2 CONC l. When the Nordic Seven-Year War broke out, he had command of the Danish Navy. Laholm Lensman from 1558 (the charge) - He hit several enemy attacks back in 1565 and 1568. He himself owned the manor Urup and got in 1536 Harritsbor
2 CONC g County, which he later exchanged with Helsingborg Len. Peder Skram was written in 1548 to Helsingborg Len and Landskrone castle, and he laid the foundation stone of Landskrone castle in 1549.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Skram (born about 1502, dead July 11, 1581) was a Danish admiral and naval hero, born on his father's estate in Urup near Horsens in Jutland.
2 CONT
2 CONT His first service in the Swedish War was for Christian II at the Battle of Brann Church in 1518. In the battle of Uppsala two years later, he saved the life of the standard carrier. For his services during this war he got a cargo 
2 CONC in Norway, where he settled with his wife Elsebeth Krabbe. He led the fleet against Christian II in Norway in 1531. Grevefeiden [edit] In Grevefeiden from 1534 to 1536 his reputation as a sailor was already established and he was 
2 CONC sent by the Danish government to assist Gustav Vasa, who at that time was allied with Christian III, in battle against Lübeck and the Danish throne-dated Count Christoffer. Peder Skram helped organize the Swedish fleet during the 
2 CONC war. The effort reduced his influence in the Baltic Sea area, and by the coronation in 1536, Peder Skram became the nobility for the effort. He also took part in the king's council and contributed in the fight against German domin
2 CONC ation. New command [edit] Peder Skram resigned as an admiral in 1555, but seven years later he again took command, now in connection with the seven-year war, when King Frederik offered him it. He was subsequently followed by Herlu
2 CONC f Trolle and retired. Twice the Swedes tried to beleive him at the castle of Laholm, where he lived, but he managed. His property in Halland was also raided several times. When he died at his age, Urup, he had long been given the 
2 CONC nickname "Denmark's dungeon". [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:TcyNVRQMSf0J:www.djoef-forlag.dk/media/21ecdd44-8dc3-40c9-9463-f3e6cff5e6de/Downloads/9788757401622/domme1_htm+&cd=3&hl=en&ct = clnk & gl = dk] DJ
2 CONC OEF: No. 446 • Viborg 06.06.1542 Dombog 4, Fol. 35V-36R Niels Juel's wife (Adel • Astrup, Grinderslev S., Nørre H., Viborg A.) against Peder Skram (Adel • Voldbjerg, Hee S., Hind H., Ringkøbing A.) Trade and craft mills Law of Mot
2 CONC hs: Property, Mills) • The King Present; 10 absent from council • 1st instance. Outcome: Other: New Law on Moth Lot Resume: Applicant accused defendant regarding ownership of mule bodys. • Printed: DD1, No. 97 No. 709 • Copenhagen
2 CONC  00.05.1549 Dombog 5, Fol. 246V-247V Peder Skram (nobility) against Claus Bille (nobility) Raised and possession - property (justice, settlement, property, graveyard) • King absent; 18 absent from council • 1st instance. Outcome: 
2 CONC Conciliation Summary: Appeals defendant, because it had taken a farm from Båstad Church, which Claus Rønnow had added to the church. No. 710 • Copenhagen 00.05.1549 Dombog 5, Fol. 247V-248V Peder Skram (nobility) against Claus Bil
2 CONC le (nobility) Fishing and shipping - fishing (justice, settlement, delights, fishing, dams) • King absent; 18 absent from council • 1st instance. Outcome: Conciliation Summary: Appeals defendant, because it had caused a dam to des
2 CONC troy the Arrerup Mølledam fishery. No. 711 • Copenhagen 00.05.1549 Dombog 5, Fol. 249V-250V Peder Skram (nobility) against Claus Bille (nobility) Forest m.v. - hunting (hunting, commission, hunting, royal branding)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peder_Skram
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Skram (født ca. 1503 - 11. juli 1581). Rigsråd, admiral. Gift med Elsebeth, der var datter af rigsmarsk Tyge Krabbe. I løbet af deres lange ægteskab fik Peder Skram og Elsebe Krabbe i alt 18 børn; 7 sønner og 11 døtre. Tre a
2 CONC f døtrene døde ved fødslen og kun én af sønnerne og syv af døtrene overlevede deres forældre. Alene i 1566 døde fire af deres sønner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deltog med Henrik Gøje i felttog i Sverige og frelste ved Uppsala Mogens Gyldenstierne. Da Christian 2. var fordrevet, var Peder Skram med ved belejringen af København i 1523.
2 CONT
2 CONT I 1532 sejlede han med en lille flåde til Norge for at finde Christian 2.'s 5 skibe. Disse opbragte han ved Tønsberg og undsatte Mogens Gyldenstierne på Akershus.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hertug Christian sendte ham efter anmodning fra Gustav Vasa til Stockholm i 1535 for at kommandere den svenske flåde, der sammen med danske og preussiske skibe skulle bryde Lübecks overmagt. Blev leder af alle flådeafdelingerne, h
2 CONC julpet af den svenske admiral Per Månsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Efter at have jaget modstanderens flåde på flugt ved Bornholm, fortsatte han til Lillebælt, hvor han ødelagde en del fjendtlige skibe. Hermed sikrede han Johan Rantzaus overførsel af tropper til Sjælland efter sejren i Slaget ved 
2 CONC Øksnebjerg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Skram indtog herefter Langeland og Korsør. Fra juli 1535 blokerede han med flåden København og Malmø. Han blev såret, men vendte tilbage til blokaden og deltog heri ind til overgivelsen 29. juli 1536.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ved Christian 3.'s kroning 1537 blev han slået til ridder og i 1539 optaget i rigsrådet. Da Den Nordiske Syvårskrig i 1563 brød ud, havde han kommandoen over den danske flåde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lensmand på Laholm fra 1558 (afgiftslen) - han slog flere fjendtlige angreb tilbage i 1565 og 1568.
2 CONT
2 CONT Selv ejede han herregården Urup og fik i 1536 Harritsborg len, som han senere samme år ombyttede med Helsingborg Len. Peder Skram skrives i 1548 til Helsingborg Len og Landskrone slot, og han lagde grundstenen til Landskrone slot 
2 CONC i 1549.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Peder Skram, (født ca. 1502, død 11. juli 1581) var en dansk admiral og sjøhelt, født på sin fars gods i Urup nær Horsens i Jylland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans første tjeneste i svenskekrigen var for Christian II i slaget ved Brannkyrka i 1518. I slaget ved Uppsala to år senere berget han livet til standardbæreren. For sine tjenester i denne krigen fikk han et gods i Norge, hvor han
2 CONC  bosatte seg med sin kone Elsebeth Krabbe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han førte flåten mot Christian II i Norge 1531.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grevefeiden [rediger]
2 CONT
2 CONT I Grevefeiden 1534 til 1536 var hans ry som sjømann allerede etablert og han ble sendt av den danske regjeringen for å assistere Gustav Vasa, som på den tid var alliert med Christian III, i kamp mot Lübeck og den danske tronpreten
2 CONC dent grev Christoffer. Peder Skram hjalp med å organisere den svenske flåten i løpet av krigen. Innsatsen reduserte hansaveldets innflytelse i Østersjøområdet, og ved kroningen i 1536 ble Peder Skram adlet som takk for innsatsen. 
2 CONC Han fikk også plass i kongens råd og bidro der i kampen mot tysk dominans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ny kommando [rediger]
2 CONT
2 CONT Peder Skram sa fra seg vervet som admiral i 1555, men sju år senere tok han igjen kommando, nå i forbindelse med sjuårskrigen, da kong Frederik I tilbød ham den. Han ble siden etterfulgt av Herluf Trolle og trakk seg tilbake. To g
2 CONC anger prøvde svenskene å beleire ham på slottet Laholm, hvor han bodde, men han klarte seg. Hans gods i Halland ble også raidet flere ganger.
2 CONT
2 CONT Da han i høy alder døde på sitt gods Urup hadde han for lengst fått tilnavnet «Danmarks våghals».
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:TcyNVRQMSf0J:www.djoef-forlag.dk/media/21ecdd44-8dc3-40c9-9463-f3e6cff5e6de/Downloads/9788757401622/domme1_htm+&cd=3&hl=en&ct=clnk&gl=dk] DJOEF:
