1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Per_Gustafsson_Ban%C3%A9r '''Per Gustafsson Banér'''], also known as Peder Gustafsson Banér (28 June 1588 – 13 July 1644) was a Swedish nobleman and member of the Privy Council of Swe
2 CONC den.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Banér was the son''' of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustaf_Ban%C3%A9r Gustaf Banér] who was one of the noblemen executed in 1600 at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Link%C3%B6ping_Bloodbath Linköping Bloodbath], and Kristi
2 CONC na Sture, daughter of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Svante_Stensson_Sture Svante Stensson Sture].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He became a kammarjunkare''' to king [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustavus_Adolphus_of_Sweden Gustavus Adolphus] in 1611, and followed the king on his incursion into Skåne in 1612. At the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle
2 CONC _of_Vittsj%C3%B6 Battle of Vittsjö], Banér helped save the king from drowning, and the grateful king made him a chamberlain and conferred on him the estates of Banér's uncle Sten Axelsson Banér, who had also been executed at the L
2 CONC inköping bloodbath. In 1617, when Gustavus Adolphus was crowned, Banér was knighted.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He married Hebbla Fleming''' in 1615. Their son Gustaf Persson Banér was born in 1618. Hebbla Fleming died in 1639.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From 1622 to 1624, Banér''' was governor of Estonia and in 1625 he was made a member of the Privy Council. He was Lawspeaker for Öland and Östergötland from 1627.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His estate included''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eken%C3%A4s_Castle Ekenäs Castle], which he rebuilt into a Renaissance style castle between 1630 and 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Banér served under''' [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_Oxenstierna Axel Oxenstierna] and acted as Oxenstierna's deputy when the latter assisted Gustavus Adolphus in Germany during the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_Oxen
2 CONC stierna#1630%E2%80%931636:_Oxenstierna_in_the_Thirty_Years'_War Thirty Years' War]. Oxenstierna was however not entirely satisfied with Banér, who was often ill and suffered from bouts of melancholia, and did not act with sufficie
2 CONC nt force to please his superiors.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 20 June 1644, Banér''' was suddenly taken ill with a fever (blague), and he died three weeks later, on 13 July. He was buried in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riddarholm_Church Riddarholmskyrkan].
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ban%C3%A9r_nr_22#TAB_15 '''Peder Banér'''], född 1588-06-28 på Djursholm, † 1644-07-12 i Stockholm av brännsjukan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Vid tjugutre års''' ålder utnämnd till kammarjunkare hos Gustaf II Adolf åtföljde konungen till danska kriget där hans första bragd var att med yttersta fara för eget liv söka rädda Gustaf Adolf, som under träffningen på Wittsj
2 CONC ön kommit under isen. Peder föll själv i vattnet och var nära att drunkna, men räddades av sin broder Nils, under det konungen uppdrogs av Upplandsryttaren Tomas Larsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peder blev för sin''' behjärtade handling slagen till riddare vid Gustaf Adolfs kröning 1617. Han nyttjades sedan i några diplomatiska värv, utnämndes till riksråd 1625 och två år därefter till lagman öfver Öland och Östergötla
2 CONC nd. Inom rådet blev han 1626 insatt i kansliet och tjänstgjorde under Axel Oxenstiernas frånvaro i diplomatiska värv som vice kansler, men vann i denna egenskap föga berömmelse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sjuklig till både kropp''' och själ, kom han på spänd fot med åtskilliga av sina ämbetsbröder, ej minst Axel Oxenstierna och tillhörde den mot denne fientliga fraktionen av rådet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1615-08-23''' i Stockholm med friherrinnan '''Hebbla Fleming''', dotter av riksrådet och riksmarsken [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Fleming_nr_4#TAB_8 Claes Fleming] och grevinnan [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealo
2 CONC gi/Stenbock_nr_12#TAB_2 Ebba Stenbock].
