1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Kristina Johansdotter Elofsönernas ätt=
2 CONT
2 CONT * She made her will during a serious illness 6/7 1293, and then chose her camp city from the preaching brothers in Sigtuna. She had owned property in Gräsgård's hd which her husband sold. Against receipt, her husband returned his 
2 CONC morning gift goods in Östergötland. and left to his father and his words estate in Aska hd in Östergötland, also owned estate on Fånön in Löts sn in Trögds hd in Uppland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==SDHK No: [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?ValdSortering=DatumStigande&PageSize=20&Sokord=Kristina&EndastDigitaliserat=False&FacettLimits=IfjiTQ%3A0&AvanceradSok=True&page=35&FacettState=undefined%3Ac%7C&postid=sdhk_1678&tab=post#tab
2 CONC  '''1678''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/1678.pdf '''Dating: 1295 November 4 Place:  of issue Sigtuna''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Elofsson, Johan Ingevaldsson on behalf of Folke Jonsson and this Folke himself, Filip (Finvidsson) of Rumby on behalf of his children, '''Magnus Gregersson on behalf of his wife and Inge Bursvenannounces that at the funeral 
2 CONC of Mrs. Kristina, Johan Elofsson's daughter, as guardian of the said Kristina's heirs approved and confirmed her testamentary appointment concerning the farms Edö and Öna with Åmme mill and meadows in Hammar (in Närke), which she 
2 CONC handed over to her husband Birger Petersson for the redemption of the testamentary gifts in said will,''' and further ordered and confirmed that Kristina's heirs shall not claim Mrs Kristina's legal inheritance from Mrs Birger's p
2 CONC roperty or bother him or his heirs regarding it. Birger Petersson, for his part, declares the wife's heirs free from all claims on the inheritance from the wife's property that would legally accrue to him. The witnesses were Dompr
2 CONC ost Andreas in Uppsala, Mr. Röd and his brother Mr. Orestes (!), Mr. Karl Erlandsson, Mr. Johan Ängel, senior lecturer Israel in Sigtuna, lawyer Håkan, Eskil "skielghi", Karl "høcher", Olof in Ekeby, Johannes "gasabogh", Johannes 
2 CONC "chobucher", Olof from "languthoru" and Sixten. Sealants are the issuers, Provost Andreas and Messrs. Röd, Orestes and Karl Erlandsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''SEAL''' 8 of 11 preserved: 1, 4, 10, 11 spiritual, damaged; 7, 8, 9 dropped out; 2, 3, 5, 6, less injured. Nr 1: domprost Andreas Andersson Ands (Sv. Sig. II: 93, 95), nr 2: Johan Ingevaldssons (Sv. Sig. III: 91), nr 3: Filip
2 CONC  Finvidssons (Sv. Sig. III: 97), nr 4: kanik Karl Erlandssons (Sv. Sig. II: 123), nr 5: Magnus Gregerssons (Sv. Sig. II: 98), nr 6: Röd Keldorssons (Sv. Sig. III: 99), nr 10: kanik Karl Erlandssons (? Cf. no. 4, above; Sv. Sig. II
2 CONC : 123), nr 11: lektor Israels i Sigtuna (Sv. Sig. II: 114).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://books.google.com/books?id=MpDiGKG4FSsC&pg=PA241&lpg=PA241&dq=Ulf+Gudmarsson&source=bl&ots=Db4XDvDO7g&sig=zNg6WibMrPAr_tG9eYklZwkeIqA&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjL7JLLvODWAhVC7SYKHc6GBWcQ6AEILjAB#v=onepage&q=Ulf%20Gudmarsson&f
2 CONC =false
2 CONT * Printed regest
2 CONT * J. Liedgren in RA's exhibition catalog 1973, p. 2
2 CONT * Literature and commentary, 1 No. 1: provost Andreas Andersson Ands (Sv. sig. II:93, 95), no. 2: Johan Ingevaldssons (Sv. sig. III:91), no. 3: Filip Finvidssons (Sv. sig. III:97), no. 4: kanik Karl Erlandssons (Sv. sig. II:123), 
2 CONC no. 5: Magnus Gregerssons (Sv. sig. II:98), no. 6: Röd Keldorssons (Sv. sig. III:99), no. 10: kanik Karl Erlandssons (? Cf. no. 4, above; Sv. sig. II:123), no. 11: lecturer Israels in Sigtuna (Sv. sig. II:114).
2 CONT See 12930706 (DS 1095).
