2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gudmund Pedersson to Örbyhus in Vendels parish,''' Uppsala county, which he obtained through his marriage, but was forced to give up, first half the farm to his brother-in-law Didrik Myntmästare by King Gustaf's judgment on 152
2 CONC 5-04-22 and then, after the king switched to his brother-in-law's share, also the other half to the king s. å. in Sept. in return for two farms in Östergötland and three farms near Uppsala 12 . Wrote to Ekenäs in Örtomta parish, Ö
2 CONC stergötland county 1531-09-29, when the council ruled for a settlement between him and his brother-in-law, in Brita Vasa's 2nd marriage, Matts Persson Upplänning in an inheritance dispute on behalf of their wife 1. Must have owned
2 CONC  Skravestad in Örtomta parish. Enumerated among the men in Östergötland who were required to serve in armor at the gun inspection in Linköping 2 1537-01-15, but not named after that. He is said to have carried half a lion in the c
2 CONC oat of arms. 3 . '''Married to Märta Christersdotter Vasa , in 1531 the Riksdag and chieftain at Kalmar Castle Christer Johansson Vasa and Dordi Knutsdotter Banér were still alive . On her dubious birth see: Historiskt Bibliotek 1
2 CONC 877 part 4, ss. 400–402.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
