2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christer Gudmundsson .''' (son of Gudmund Pedersson, table 1), to Skravestad in Örtomta parish and Elltorp 4 (now Sjöberga) in Björsäters parish, both in Östergötland county. Was present at the mustering with the savior in Ös
2 CONC tergötland in 1562 5 . Submitted the declaration of allegiance to Duke Johan 1568-08-00 6 . Submitted list of goods for the 1579 armory 4 . Seems to have lived until 1586-11-00, when he is entered in the register of Sweden's nobil
2 CONC ity. Married to Ingeborg Johansdotter 
2 CONT * '''Johan Gudmundsson .''' Ship's chief officer. Died 1570. (son of Gudmund Pedersson, table 1), to Hällerstad in Östra Ryds parish, Brånnestad in Gistads parish and Torlunda and Klinga in Löts parish, all in Östergötland county,
2 CONC  which farms he and his brothers received from King Erik on 12/01/1561 for the consideration in Fittja village in Lagunda district Uppsala county, which the council awarded to their mother for Örby 7 . Sealed among the nobility, K
2 CONC ing Gustaf I's will in 1560 and the estates' grant in 1561 (when he signed himself to Skravestad). Was present at the mustering with the savior in Östergötland in 1563 5 . Ship's chief officer. Died 1570-06-15 on the ship Engeln a
2 CONC nd buried s. å. 13/7 in Österhaninge church Stockholms län, where his shield with the Ulf weapon and signature was set up. Married 1560-10-21 to his sister-in-law's sister Kerstin Marboin her 1st marriage (married 2nd 1575-06-12 a
2 CONC t Hällerstad 9 to the prefect Tyge Larsson, knighted Gyllencreutz , in his 1st marriage, died 1625), died 1603 8 , daughter of the castle law at Stegeborg, chamber councilor Truls Andersson Skrivare (Marbo) to Ravanäs, who in the 
2 CONC coat of arms brought half a lily and a star, and his 3rd wife Karin Eriksdotter Slätte (no. 97).
2 CONT * '''Erik Gudmundsson .''' Cavalry captain. Died 1564. (son of Gudmund Pedersson, table 1), to Låstad in Furingstad parish, Östergötland county and Vrangsjö in Marbäck parish, Jönköping county. Equestrian during King Erik's time. 
2 CONC Was present at the mustering with the savior in Östergötland in 1562 6 . Died in 1564 at Vrangsjö as a result of a gunshot wound, which he received in the battle at Ronneby, and buried in Marbäck's church. Married in 1555 to Ingeb
2 CONC org Marbo in her 1st marriage (married 2nd to bailiff Jöns Eriksson ( Rosenstråle ) in his 2nd marriage) 10 , daughter of the castle bailiff at Stegeborg, chamber councilor Truls Andersson. Printer (Marbo), to Ravanäs, who in the 
2 CONC coat of arms brought half a lily and a star, and his 3rd wife Karin Eriksdotter Slatte .
2 CONT
