0 @I6000000006595821603@ INDI
1 NAME Laurids /Norby/
2 GIVN Laurids
2 _MARNM Norby
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} May not have been a Sören Norby son, but rather a Norby servant. This issue is left unsettled.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July, 1525, while Bernt von Mehlen and Kristina Gyllenstierna were in Bleking with Sören Norby, King Gustav Vasa's forces attacked and captured Kalmar Castle, which at the time was held by von Mehlen. Among the castle's occupan
2 CONC ts were Nils Stensson Sture, Kristina Gyllenstierna's young son. Sometime after July and before the end of November, Leonard or Leonardus Norby (a servant and/or son of Sören Norby), Sören Norby's young daughter, and Severin Brun,
2 CONC  a Sören Norby aid, fell into Gustav Vasa's hands when the ship transporting them from Visby to Blekinge ran aground and was captured near Kalmar.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been reported that every last person at Kalmar Castle, except Nils Stensson Sture, was killed. This exception may have been influenced by the fact that King Gustav Vasa was Kristina's sister's husband. Sören Norby's daughte
2 CONC r was never seen again by her father. The fate of Leonardus Norby is unknown. Söffuerin Brun, the Norby aide, was executed in the Stockholm Market in February, 1527.
