1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Katarina Staffansdotter (Ulv)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Staffan Ulfsson Ulv af Lagnö and NN Haraldsdotter (Gren)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  '''Bengt Larsson bjälke från Västergötland,''' Married around 1391 (Had daughter Ingeborg).
2 CONT * Married: '''Carl Larsson till Frötuna,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Child with Bengt Larsson bjälke från Västergötland=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ingeborg Bengtsdotter bjälke från Västergötland,''' Daughter of Bengt Larsson (bjälke) and his second wife Katarina Staffansdotter (Ulv). First Marriage: Bengt Tomasson (Pipa) (d. before 1442). He was a well-documented squire
2 CONC  who originally held the massive family properties of Bystad (in Asker, Närke). When Bengt Pipa died, Ingeborg was left as a relatively young, highly wealthy widow in control of his properties. She Second Marriage (ca. 1442): Lars
2 CONC  Siggesson "den äldre" (Sparre). When Lars Siggesson married her, he did so specifically as the "widow of Bengt Tomasson (Pipa).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Lars Björnsson bjälke Geneology Chart=
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000225647841999&&size=large}}  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Tillbakaseende_ulv Looking back wolf, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''TAB 5'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Staffan Ulfsson (son of Ulf Philippusson,''' tab. 4). Earliest mentioned in 1357. Was district governor in Selebo hd in Södermanland at least 1365 - 1382 and the king's bailiff in Uppsala in 1366. Became a knight between 16.11.
2 CONC  1369 and 1.1. 1370 and possibly already in 1370 or 1371 and certainly no later than 1375 councilor of the realm, which he was still in 1389. His estate was Lagnö in Aspö sn. Selebo hd in Södermanland. '''Was married in 1377 to a 
2 CONC daughter of Harald Ernilsson (Gren), whose only known wife was probably the daughter of the knight and councilor of the realm Torkel Andersson (divided shield, later boat)'''. Staffan Ulfsson's '''widow Iliana Åkedolter died betwe
2 CONC en 16.3 1423 and 5.8 1424, daughter of the knight and sculler Åke Ingvarsson (boat) and Anna Gerhardsdotter ( Snakenborg ).''' Mrs. Iliana remarried in 1398 to the knight Claus Dowt, who is believed to have been knighted at King E
2 CONC rik's coronation on 17.6 1397.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Ramborg Staffansdotter.''' Earliest mentioned in 1383. Her estate was Lag-nö in Aspö sn, Selebo hd in Södermanland. Married no later than 1374 on Lagnö, whereupon she received land in Tuhundra hd in Västmanland as a dowry 
2 CONC from Ödgisl Suneson ( 3 sjöblads ), who is mentioned earliest in 1368, and died between 29.1. 1383 and 2.8. 1384. Their son, the councilor and lawman in Södermanland Mats Ödgisleson took up his grandfather's coat of arms, after wh
2 CONC ich the family was called Lillie. Ramborg probably received land in Rönö hd in Södermanland as a morning gift from the royal councillor Folke Nilsson ( Ivar Nilsson's family ) at Svanaholm in Västra Hargs sn, Vifolka hd in Östergö
2 CONC tland, who is mentioned from 1364, having previously been married to the deceased Märta Gustavsdotter ( Sparre of Vik ) in 1384.
2 CONT * 1. '''Katarina Staffansdotter.''' In 1386, she received for her life Rundholm in Vansö sn, Åkers hd in Södermanland from her fiancé Folke Karlsson ( Ekeblad from Västerfärnebo ), who died in 1387. She was still alive in 1415 and
2 CONC  was then at least since 1391 '''married to Bengt Larsson ( Lars Bjömsson's family ) at Vinäs (now Duseborg) in Gammalkils sn, Valkebo hd in Östergötland, who is mentioned from 1389 and was still alive on 3 August 1421.'''
2 CONT * 1. '''Bengta Staffansdotter.''' Mentioned as a nun in Vårfruberga monastery 1395—1400.
2 CONT * 2. '''Ulf Staffansson,''' 1405, died around 1437, district governor. See tab. 6.
2 CONT * 2. '''Kristina Staffansdotter.''' Owned land in Norra Vedbo hd in Småland, Memmings hd in Östergötland and Österrekarne hd in Södermanland. Died between 24.1. 1460 and 10.3. 1461 and wanted to be buried in Vadstena Monastery. Po
2 CONC ssibly as early as 1407 and certainly before 1418, she married the later Reichsrat Bengt Uddsson ( Vinstorpaätten ) at Vinsarp in Böne sn, Redvägs hd in Västergötland, who gave her the morning gift in Frökinds, Gudhems, Redvägs an
2 CONC d Var-tofta hd in Västergötland and Tveta hd in Småland, earliest mentioned in 1407, had the rural household in Viste and Ås hd in Västergötland, in Sundals hd in Dalsland, in Värend in Småland, in Selebo hd in Södermanland and in
2 CONC  Skåne and was killed in the winter of 1436—1437.
2 CONT * 2. '''Åke Staffansson.''' Died before 16.3 1423.
