1 OCCU Herre till Rånnum i Tunhems fs och Sjöbo i Torpa. Väpnare. Knekthövidsman. Häradshövdning i Väne härad 1540. Med i Erik XIV krig mot Danmark, Vapnare, høvitsman
1 TITL till Rånnum
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Bengt Pedersson Svenske=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Per Larsson Svenske and Cecilia Bengtsdotter Sparre
2 CONT * Bengt Svenske (son of Peder Svenske, Tab. 1. ), to Rånnum and Sjöbo. Squire. Was county chief in Väne county in 1540. Still alive in 1589, but was dead in 1597. Married to Gyrith Torstensdotter , daughter of regimental councilor
2 CONC  Torsten Brunsson ( Forstena family no. 2 ) and Anna Gudmundsdotter (ram's head) .
2 CONT * District chief in Väne district 1540. Knekthövitsman during Erik XIV's time in the war against Denmark. Was ordered to invade Norway in July 1564, took part in the campaign in Halland in 1566, was sentenced to death by King Erik
2 CONC 's council in 1567 for neglect during the war, signed up to Koberg in Lagmansereds sn (Älvsborg) in 1568, sat in the court in Väne district as late as 1582 , is taken up in fort. over Swedish nobility 1586 - Subscribes to Sjöbo. W
2 CONC as still alive in 1589 but was dead in 1597.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married to '''Gyrith Torstensdotter,''' daughter of the regiment council Torsten Brunsson (Forstena family no. 2) and Anna Gudmundsdotter (baghuvud).
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Brown,''' died childless 1616. Married to Anna Nilsdotter, daughter of the chieftain Nils Pedersson (Lilliehöök of Fårdala nr 1) and Carin Carlsdotter (Store nr 79).
2 CONT * '''Peder Bengtsson Svenske to Rånnum,''' Shepherd chief in Väne after the father in 1588 and still 1600. Was dead in 1623. Married to Margareta Kagg, daughter of the ruler Mattias Nilsson Kagg (no. 68) and his 2nd wife Elin Gust
2 CONC afsdotter (Forstenaätten).
2 CONT *''' Brita,''' lived widow in 1598, but was dead in 1616. Married to the castle law Sven Andersson (Stålhandske in Västergötland, no. 66).
2 CONT * '''Harald Bengtsson Svenske,''' was dead in 1626. Married to Elseby Pedersdotter, daughter of Peder Jensen (Dahlepil nr 663) and Elin Esbjörnsdotter.
2 CONT * '''Jakob,''' was dead in 1626
2 CONT * '''Carin,''' lived in 1616. Married to Herman in Brätte.
2 CONT *''' Elin,''' lived in 1616. Married to Gilian NN.
2 CONT * '''Anna,''' lived 1616. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - The noble family Swedish no. 258, Tab 3 - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svenske_nr_258#TAB_3
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =GEDCOM Note=
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Died after 1589. County chief Väne county. To Rånum in Tunhems sn and Sjöbo in Torpa? sn (Älvsborg). Squire. District chief in Väne district 1540. Knekthövitsman during Erik XIV's time in the war against Denmark. Was ord
2 CONC ered to invade Norway in July 1564, took part in the campaign in Halland in 1566, was sentenced to death by King Erik's council in 1567 for neglect during the war, signed up to Koberg in Lagmansereds sn (Älvsborg) in 1568, sat in 
2 CONC court in the Väne district as late as 1582 , is taken up in fort. over Swedish nobility 1586 - Subscribes to Sjöbo. Still alive in 1589 but dead in 1597. Source: G Elgenstierna
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.lennheden.com/genealogi/gunnar/000/0001/183.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * The noble family Kagg No. 68 dead.  Ancient family of salvation. Introduced in 1625. Extinct 1790-06-15. The genus has branched out into free-spirited and gruesome eaters Kagg, Tab 5 - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Kagg_n
2 CONC r_68#TAB_5
2 CONT * Introduceret pa Sveriges Riddarhus 1638 som adelig slagt nr. 184.
