1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =NN Johansdotter Lily of Värnäs=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Johan Bengtsson, Lily of Värnäs & Märta Johansdotter Ulf
2 CONT * Shield: In blue field half a lily of gold and above a spar of silver. Helmet: A half lily of gold. Uradel, which first appears in Kinds and Vartofta counties in 1413. '''The last member of the family''' marries the immortal '''P
2 CONC eder Larson Svenske''' (known 1527-1556). The weapon's tinctures are taken from the Swedish coat of arms. Introduced in 1638. Swedish Medieval Arms, p. 808
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: (1)  '''Per Larsson Svenske,''' son of Son of Lars Pedersson Svenske.
2 CONT * Married: (2) who was remarried to the vicar in Dalstorp's pastorate of Skara diocese '''Olof Haquini'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svenske_nr_258 Noble family Swedish no. 258, by Adelsvapen Genealogies]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble family Swedish no. 258, Introduced 1638 (the information about this family is uncertain)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TABLE 1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Peder Svenske .''' Died in 1534-12 at the siege of Varberg. In 1531, he received two farms in Eckerna in Tunge parish, Älvsborg county, and "in addition to the estates he added, namely Alwen, Sålanda, Bergh and Skogxtorp, which
2 CONC  he shall freely keep during his lifetime with all the rights arising from them". '''Married 1st , acc. the knight's house genealogy, with Cecilia Bengtsdotter , daughter of the squire and district chief Bengt Björnsson (a sparre)
2 CONC  and Ingrid Carlsdotter (Lake, no. 53). Married 2nd to N. N , (who was remarried to the vicar in Dalstorp's pastorate of Skara diocese Olof Haquini.)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children in marriage 1:o=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Bengt. District Chief.'''  (son of Peder Svenske, Tab. 1. ), to Rånnum and Sjöbo. Squire. Was county chief in Väne county in 1540. Still alive in 1589, but was dead in 1597. Married to Gyrith Torstensdotter , daughter of regi
2 CONC mental councilor Torsten Brunsson ( Forstena family no. 2 ) and Anna Gudmundsdotter (ram's head) .
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children in marriage 2:o=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Anders.''' "Proceeded" through his wastefulness all that the father left behind. Married: Karin Mårtensdotter Dingelvik
2 CONT * '''Petrus Petri Svenske,''' born 1525. Church pastor. Died 1591. (son of Peder Svenske, Tab. 1. ), born approx. 1525. Died 1591. Ordained priest 1559. Pastorate of Höreda and Mellby parishes of Linköping diocese 1560. Married 15
2 CONC 70 to Catharina Bröms , daughter of the nobleman Lars Bröms , No. 161, and Margareta Drake, of the old Drake family. In addition to the daughters, the couple had four sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilja_av_V%C3%A4rn%C3%A4s Lily of Värnäs]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Lilja av Värnäs or Lilja till Värnäs , is a conventional family name of a medieval savior family from Västergötland that carried a spar over half a lily in its coat of arms.  The family died out before Sweden's House of Knights wa
2 CONC s founded in 1625, which is why it was never introduced there as a form of nobility .
2 CONT
2 CONT Bengt Gjordsson is mentioned in Kinds and Vartofta districts in 1413.
2 CONT
2 CONT A daughter, Kerstin Bengtsson, married to the gunsmith Olof Christiernsson Drake from Västbo , and two of Bengt's sons are known, Krister Bengtsson and brother Johan Bengtsson to Värnäs ( Värna parish in Östergötland).
2 CONT
2 CONT No children are known from Johan's son Christiern Johansson , but the last member of the family, his daughter with an unknown name, was married to the unsaved prefect of Lysing's district Peder Larsson Svenske (known 1527-1556), a
2 CONC nd became the progenitor of the nobility Swedish number 258 which carried the coat of arms with the spar over half a lily.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svenske_nr_258#TAB_1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Jan Raneke ; Swedish Medieval Arms, p. 808
2 CONT * Nobility. ätten Svenske, No. 258 in Gabriel Anrep , Swedish nobility family tables (1858–1864), section 
2 CONT * Medieval families in Sjuhärad - Medieval families in Sjuhärad
2 CONT * roskildehistorie.dk - https://www.roskildehistorie.dk/stamtavler/adel/svenske/Svenske/Svenske.htm
2 CONT * Lilja av Värnäs eller Lilja till Värnäs, - https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilja_av_V%C3%A4rn%C3%A4s
2 CONT * /RH 20230128
2 CONT
2 CONT
